Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): preserve tab content across adaptive navigation
 hosts

Shared content factory and regression with Mihon 0079. Preview.30 keeps one Activity across folding, but its trace still shows the library leaving at offsets 36038 / 21254 and each replacement entering at zero. HomeScreen independently composes TabContent under its rail and bottom-bar branches. Hoist one owner-scoped movable composition and invoke it in either host, keeping remembered list state and active content while receiving the latest lambda and locals. Navigation appearance, tablet policy, rendering diagnostics and gesture logic are unchanged. Test six regular/subcomposed host moves with internally remembered list state, identity, disposal count, updated content and bottom padding; replacing the navigation owner must still dispose/reset the body. This addresses a confirmed tab-lifetime defect, not proof that all perceived compositor stutter is resolved.
